# Zephyr CI/CD Tool - Product Requirements Document (PRD)

## Product Overview
Zephyr is a modern Continuous Integration and Continuous Deployment (CI/CD) platform designed to streamline software development workflows through automation. With a focus on user experience and reliability, Zephyr aims to simplify the complexity of CI/CD processes while providing powerful capabilities for development teams of all sizes.

## Target Audience
- Software development teams
- DevOps engineers
- QA teams
- Engineering managers
- Independent developers

## Business Objectives
1. Provide an intuitive and powerful CI/CD solution that reduces time-to-deployment
2. Simplify the configuration and maintenance of automated pipelines
3. Increase visibility into build and deployment processes
4. Improve team collaboration through transparent workflows
5. Reduce errors in software delivery through consistent automation

## Technical Stack
- **Frontend**: React with TypeScript
- **Backend API**: Go
- **Pipeline Execution Engine**: Python
- **Database**: PostgreSQL
- **Caching**: Redis
- **Containerization**: Docker
- **Orchestration**: Kubernetes

## Product Requirements

### 1. Pipeline Configuration UI

#### 1.1 Visual Pipeline Builder
- **Priority**: High
- **Description**: Drag-and-drop interface for creating and editing pipeline configurations
- **Requirements**:
  - Support for drag-and-drop configuration of pipeline stages and steps
  - Visual representation of pipeline flow and dependencies
  - Ability to save pipeline configurations as templates
  - Version history of pipeline configurations

#### 1.2 YAML Configuration Editor
- **Priority**: Medium
- **Description**: Text editor for direct YAML pipeline configuration
- **Requirements**:
  - Syntax highlighting for YAML
  - Real-time validation of configuration syntax
  - Side-by-side view with visual pipeline representation
  - Auto-completion suggestions

#### 1.3 Configuration Templates
- **Priority**: Medium
- **Description**: Pre-defined pipeline templates for common use cases
- **Requirements**:
  - Library of templates for popular frameworks and languages
  - Community-contributed templates marketplace
  - Template customization and forking capabilities

### 2. Pipeline Execution Engine

#### 2.1 Container-Based Execution
- **Priority**: High
- **Description**: Run pipeline steps in isolated Docker containers
- **Requirements**:
  - Support for custom Docker images
  - Container caching for improved performance
  - Resource allocation controls (CPU, memory)
  - Security scanning of container images

#### 2.2 Parallel Execution
- **Priority**: High
- **Description**: Ability to run pipeline steps in parallel when possible
- **Requirements**:
  - Automatic dependency resolution
  - Configurable concurrency limits
  - Resource-aware scheduling

#### 2.3 Caching System
- **Priority**: Medium
- **Description**: Cache build artifacts and dependencies between pipeline runs
- **Requirements**:
  - Configurable caching policies
  - Automatic cache invalidation
  - Support for distributed caching

#### 2.4 Job Scheduling and Queueing
- **Priority**: Medium
- **Description**: Intelligent scheduling of pipeline jobs
- **Requirements**:
  - Priority-based job queue
  - Fair scheduling algorithm
  - Support for scheduled (cron-like) pipeline executions

### 3. Real-Time Pipeline Monitoring

#### 3.1 Pipeline Dashboard
- **Priority**: High
- **Description**: Central dashboard showing status of all pipelines
- **Requirements**:
  - Real-time status updates
  - Filtering and sorting options
  - Team and project views
  - Historical pipeline execution statistics

#### 3.2 Log Viewer
- **Priority**: High
- **Description**: Real-time log streaming for pipeline execution
- **Requirements**:
  - Live log streaming
  - Log filtering and search
  - Log highlighting for errors and warnings
  - Log export functionality

#### 3.3 Metrics and Analytics
- **Priority**: Medium
- **Description**: Performance metrics and insights for pipelines
- **Requirements**:
  - Build time trends
  - Success/failure rates
  - Resource utilization metrics
  - Custom metric dashboards

### 4. Notifications

#### 4.1 Integration Channels
- **Priority**: Medium
- **Description**: Support for various notification channels
- **Requirements**:
  - Email notifications
  - Slack integration
  - Microsoft Teams integration
  - Webhook support for custom integrations

#### 4.2 Notification Rules
- **Priority**: Medium
- **Description**: Configurable rules for when to send notifications
- **Requirements**:
  - Event-based notification rules
  - User and team subscription settings
  - Notification templates customization

### 5. Version Control Integration

#### 5.1 GitHub Integration
- **Priority**: High
- **Description**: Deep integration with GitHub repositories
- **Requirements**:
  - OAuth authentication
  - Repository webhook configuration
  - Pull request status updates
  - Branch protection rule integration

#### 5.2 GitLab Integration
- **Priority**: Medium
- **Description**: Integration with GitLab repositories
- **Requirements**:
  - OAuth authentication
  - Repository webhook configuration
  - Merge request status updates

#### 5.3 Bitbucket Integration
- **Priority**: Medium
- **Description**: Integration with Bitbucket repositories
- **Requirements**:
  - OAuth authentication
  - Repository webhook configuration
  - Pull request status updates

### 6. Authentication and Authorization

#### 6.1 User Authentication
- **Priority**: High
- **Description**: Secure user authentication system
- **Requirements**:
  - Email/password authentication
  - OAuth integration (GitHub, GitLab, Google)
  - Two-factor authentication
  - SSO integration (SAML, OIDC)

#### 6.2 Role-Based Access Control
- **Priority**: High
- **Description**: Granular permissions system
- **Requirements**:
  - Predefined roles (Admin, Developer, Viewer)
  - Custom roles with granular permissions
  - Project-level access controls
  - Pipeline-specific permissions

### 7. API and Extensibility

#### 7.1 RESTful API
- **Priority**: Medium
- **Description**: Comprehensive API for programmatic control
- **Requirements**:
  - Full coverage of UI functionality
  - API versioning
  - Rate limiting
  - Comprehensive documentation

#### 7.2 Plugin System
- **Priority**: Low
- **Description**: Extensibility through plugins
- **Requirements**:
  - Plugin marketplace
  - Custom step development SDK
  - Integration plugins for third-party services

## Non-Functional Requirements

### 1. Performance
- Pipeline execution startup time under 10 seconds
- UI response time under 200ms for 95% of requests
- Support for concurrent execution of at least 100 pipeline jobs

### 2. Scalability
- Horizontal scaling for all components
- Support for distributed execution across multiple nodes
- Ability to handle at least 1000 pipeline executions per day

### 3. Reliability
- 99.9% uptime for core services
- Automated recovery from common failure scenarios
- No data loss in case of system failures

### 4. Security
- Encrypted data at rest and in transit
- Secure handling of secrets and credentials
- Regular security audits and vulnerability scanning

### 5. Compliance
- Audit logging for all system actions
- Data retention policies configuration
- GDPR compliance features

## Success Metrics
1. Average pipeline execution time reduction
2. Build success rate improvement
3. Time saved in pipeline configuration
4. User adoption and retention rates
5. Reduction in deployment issues

